= CHIEF COMPLAINTS
1. Difficulty in breathing for 1 month.
2. Swelling in both legs for 1 month.

// #vspace(1em)

= HISTORY
*History of present illness:* According to the statement of the patient, he was reasonably well 1 month back. He then started experiencing difficulty in breathing (dyspnea) which has been progressively worsening. The breathing difficulty significantly exacerbates when lying flat (orthopnea), often forcing him to sit upright to breathe comfortably. He concurrently noticed swelling in his legs (pedal edema) over the same duration, which typically worsens towards the end of the day.

*To rule out respiratory causes (Asthma/COPD):* There is no history of chronic persistent cough, wheezing, excessive sputum production, or seasonal variations of symptoms. There is no reported history of childhood asthma or prolonged exposure to biomass fuel/heavy smoking.

*To rule out renal and hepatic causes:* There is no history of facial puffiness, swelling around the eyes (periorbital edema) especially in the morning, frothy urine, or decreased urine output (oliguria), which makes a primary renal cause less likely. Furthermore, there is no history of yellowish discoloration of the eyes or urine (jaundice), abdominal distension (ascites) preceding the leg swelling, hematemesis, or altered bowel habits, lowering the suspicion for chronic liver disease.

*History of past illness:* He is a known patient of Diabetes Mellitus (DM) for [...] years, Hypertension (HTN) for [...] years, and Angina for [...] years. Notably, he suffered a Myocardial Infarction (MI) 5 years ago.

*Family history:* His father was a known diabetic and passed away due to a Myocardial Infarction (MI). 

*Personal history:* [Inquire and document smoking/alcohol habits].

*Drug and treatment history:* [Document current medications for DM, HTN, and IHD, e.g., anti-hypertensives, oral hypoglycemic agents/insulin, anti-platelets, and nitrates].

