= SYSTEMIC EXAMINATION

== Cardiovascular System (Pre-cordium)
- *Inspection:* [Apical impulse visible or not, any precordial bulging].
- *Palpation:* [Position of apex beat, presence of thrills or heaves].
- *Auscultation:* Heart sounds reveal a *gallop rhythm*. A prominent *third heart sound (S3)* is heard.

== Respiratory System
- *Auscultation:* Bilateral *basal crepitations* (crackles) are present, which do not clear with coughing.
- *Percussion/Palpation:* [Normal resonant notes globally, except possibly dull at bases if effusion is present].

== Examination of other systems
- *Gastrointestinal (Abdomen):* [Check for tender hepatomegaly or ascites].
- *Nervous System:* Intact, no gross abnormalities detected.

