= SALIENT FEATURES
A [...] year-old male, known to have Diabetes Mellitus for [...] years, Hypertension for [...] years, and Angina for [...] years, with a past history of Myocardial Infarction 5 years ago, presents with progressive dyspnea, orthopnea, and bilateral pedal edema for the last 1 month. Family history is highly positive for premature cardiovascular disease and DM. 

On examination, the patient prefers a sitting decubitus. Bilateral pitting pedal edema is noted. Cardiovascular examination is significant for an S3 gallop rhythm. Respiratory examination reveals bilateral basal crepitations. 

*My provisional diagnosis is* Congestive Heart Failure (Left and Right ventricular failure)